{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q414999","formula":"AuTe₂","hill":"AuTe2","elements":["Te","Au"],"composition":{"Au":1.0,"Te":2.0},"names":{"en":"Calaverite","ru":"Калаверит","uk":"Калаверит"},"descriptions":{"en":"Calaverite, or gold telluride, is an uncommon telluride of gold, a metallic mineral with the chemical formula AuTe2, with approximately 3% of the gold replaced by silver. It was first discovered in Calaveras County, California in 1861, and was named for the county in 1868. The mineral often has a metallic luster, and its color may range from a silvery white to a brassy yellow.","ru":"Калаверит — редкий гидротермальный минерал, по составу теллурид золота. Впервые был обнаружен в округе Калаверас (Калифорния, США) в 1861 году, откуда и получил своё название. Химическая формула — AuTe2.","uk":"Калаверит (рос. калаверит; англ. calaverite; нім."},"fame":23,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-1662","atoms":6,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[4.148,0.0,0.0],[-2.074,3.593,0.0],[0.0,0.0,5.064]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":2.074,"y":1.198,"z":3.991,"el":"Te"},{"x":0.0,"y":2.395,"z":1.073,"el":"Te"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":2.532,"el":"Au"},{"x":-2.074,"y":3.593,"z":2.532,"el":"Au"},{"x":4.148,"y":0.0,"z":2.532,"el":"Au"},{"x":2.074,"y":3.593,"z":2.532,"el":"Au"}],"bonds":[[0,2,1],[0,4,1],[0,5,1],[1,2,1],[1,3,1],[1,5,1]],"cellOrigin":[0,0,0]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q414999","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calaverite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%9A%D0%B0%D0%BB%D0%B0%D0%B2%D0%B5%D1%8